{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012WbcqZ7pswuWWEPNkh1SHY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Codebase analysis for storage abstraction","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:codebase-analyst","prompt":"You are being dispatched as part of a SpecKit clarify consensus round.\n\nQuestion to resolve:\nQ1: Should we follow the existing repository pattern in src/storage/ or introduce a new abstraction for the new resource type?\n\nYour job: Analyze the existing codebase and answer from the perspective of established code patterns and conventions. Focus on:\n1. What pattern(s) does src/storage/ currently use? Is there a consistent repository pattern, and how is it structured?\n2. How are existing resource types implemented in src/storage/? What conventions are followed (interfaces, base classes, file layout, naming)?\n3. Would the new resource type fit cleanly into the existing pattern, or are there structural reasons it would not?\n4. Is there precedent in the codebase for introducing a new abstraction when adding a resource, or has every new resource extended the existing pattern?\n\nReturn a structured answer with:\n- Recommendation (follow existing pattern OR introduce new abstraction)\n- Confidence level (high / medium / low)\n- File-level evidence with paths and line numbers\n- Any caveats or edge cases the synthesizer should know about\n\nKeep your response under ~400 words. Evidence-grounded only — if src/storage/ does not exist or the pattern is unclear, say so explicitly rather than speculating."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
